The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```java
if (arena.isRunning()) {
    if (lockFoodLevel) {
        event.setCancelled(true);
    }
}
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the food level lock is applied to all players when the arena is running and the lock is enabled, without checking if the player is actually in the arena. This results in unintended effects on players outside the arena.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
if (arena.inArena(p) && lockFoodLevel) {
    event.setCancelled(true);
}
```
Reason:
The fix adds a check to ensure that the player is in the arena before applying the food level lock. This prevents the food level change from being cancelled for players who are not in the arena, thus resolving the unintended consequences for players outside the arena.

